Z||000011||fropuff||10-24-2000||08:43 PM||||I agree.  All common sense.  I'm not 16 yet, but there's a girl in my class that shouldn't have gotten her license.  She failed the parallel parking, 90 degree parking, and the perpendicular parking, but still got it.  She hit cones, which are CARS in real life!  That's how the rules have changed.  I'm going to do my 6 hours of behind-the-wheel on Thursday and next Monday.  You can't really fail that, unless you get into an accident, and then it's 18 till I get my license.  Hope that doesn't happen.  Congrats, Blayde!||||reg||1
